  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-030">Every compose event on the bus MUST use a typed discriminant in the union — zero `as any`. This is the core contract fix (gap 5.2).</constraint>
    <constraint source="no-invented-discriminants">Do NOT reintroduce the retracted invented names compose_action_request / compose_edit_apply_request (design §7.2 / Spike 0 forbid them). Extend the EXISTING discriminants in compose-contracts.ts. Do NOT change the runtime contract of the already-shipped compose_selection_offer / compose_assistant_insert flows.</constraint>
    <constraint source="correct-pane">Receivers live on the pane that OWNS the reaction (ContextPaneController for context surfacing, the Assistant/Conversation controller for conversation reactions) — NOT a log-only handler on ComposeWorkspace. ComposeWorkspace emits/relays; it is not the terminal cross-pane handler.</constraint>
    <constraint source="reuse-070">This task supersedes 070 — fold 070's intent in; do NOT leave a parallel 070 implementation. One coherent coordination layer, not two (Component Justification §11).</constraint>
    <constraint source="real-bus-test">The forcing function MUST use the REAL PaneEventBus (not a mocked bus) and assert a cross-pane effect (emit on pane A → observable reaction on pane B). An isolated unit test that only checks a handler in isolation does NOT satisfy the project E2E definition-of-done row 3 (mounted + reachable).</constraint>
    <constraint source="no-defer">Build Flows 3/4/6 in this pass; do NOT stub them or file deferrals for in-scope flows. 072 (Doc Q&A) inherits this Context surfacing (Flow 6) — leave it consumable, but building 072 itself is out of scope.</constraint>
    <constraint source="no-http">This is a client-only coordination task — no BFF/endpoint changes. If a flow genuinely needs a server round-trip, that is an escalation, not a silent BFF edit.</constraint>
  </constraints>

